- @page_title = "Support"

= render PageHeaderComponent.new(title: "Support", back_href: native_app? ? nil : today_path, back_label: "Back to today")

= render CardComponent.new(class: "p-6 mb-4") do
  .legal-copy
    %h2 Getting help
    %p
      Email
      %a.text-primary.underline{href: "mailto:hello@tally.quest"} hello@tally.quest
      and you'll get a reply from the person who built Tally. Include what you
      were doing and what happened; a screenshot helps.

    %h2 A food's calories look wrong
    %p
      Most foods come from Open Food Facts, a community-maintained database, so
      entries can be incomplete or out of date — and manufacturers change
      recipes without changing the barcode. Create your own food with the
      correct numbers and Tally will prefer yours in future searches.

    %h2 A barcode isn't recognised
    %p
      That product isn't in Open Food Facts yet. Add it as your own food, and
      consider contributing it to
      %a.text-primary.underline{href: "https://world.openfoodfacts.org"} Open Food Facts
      so the next person finds it.

    %h2 The scanner won't open
    %p
      Tally needs camera access. Check Settings → Tally → Camera on your device.
      Barcodes can also be typed in by hand if the camera can't read one.

    %h2 I forgot my password
    %p
      Use "Forgot password?" on the login screen. The reset email arrives within
      a few minutes — check your spam folder before emailing about it.

    %h2 Deleting your account
    %p
      Settings → Delete account. It takes effect immediately and erases
      everything you have logged. Want a copy of your data first? Email the
      address above and ask.

    %h2 Tally is not medical advice
    %p
      Tally adds up numbers you enter; it is not a clinician and gives no
      medical, nutritional or dietary advice. Speak to a qualified professional
      before changing what you eat — especially if you are pregnant, managing a
      medical condition, or have a history of disordered eating.
